  "theorem_level_results": {
    "lift_update": "For a prescribed rise word, if H_s=(3^s*rho_s+A_s-2^s)/2^(s+1), then the appended digit d_s selects the unique b_s in {0,1} satisfying b_s == 1+H_s+d_s (mod 2), and rho_(s+1)=rho_s+b_s*2^(s+1).",
    "binary_digit_identity": "rho_s = 1 + sum_{j=0}^{s-1} b_j*2^(j+1); the lift bits are exactly the successive binary digits of the required starting residue above its forced odd least-significant bit.",
    "normalized_update": "theta_s=rho_s/2^(s+1) satisfies theta_(s+1)=(theta_s+b_s)/2.",
    "bounded_range_locking": "For 1<=M<=U, let B=floor(log_2 U), equivalently 2^(B+1)>U. If M realizes B prescribed exact-r=1 rises, then M=rho_B. Any further compatible extension must keep the same residue and therefore has lift bits b_B=b_(B+1)=...=0.",
    "candidate_compression": "At B=floor(log_2 U), starts in [L,U] surviving B rises are at most 20*J_B(L,U)+1. Moreover J_s(L,U)<=9*s*(ceil(log_10((U+19)/L))+1), so the explicit lock-depth candidate bound is 180*B*(ceil(log_10((U+19)/L))+1)+1."
  },
